-- title:
--   Lemma 3.2 — the greedy sparse-simplex method is monotone, f(xᵏ⁺¹) ≤ f(xᵏ), with equality iff xᵏ = xᵏ⁺¹ is a CW-minimum
-- statement:
--   Let $f:\mathbb R^n\to\mathbb R$ be continuously differentiable and bounded below (Assumption 1), let $0<s<n$ be an integer, and let $(x^k)_{k\ge0}$ be a sequence generated by the greedy sparse-simplex method for (P). Then for every $k\ge0$,
--   $$f(x^{k+1})\le f(x^k),$$
--   and equality holds if and only if $x^k=x^{k+1}$ and $x^k$ is a coordinate-wise minimum of (P) (Definition 2.4).
--
--   The lemma records that the method generates a nonincreasing sequence of function values and gets stuck only at CW-minima. It is the first step of the proof of Theorem 3.3.
--
--   **Formalization Note** A STOP of the method is modelled by $x^{k+1}=x^k$, so the sequence is defined for every $k$. Assumption 1 is the paper's standing assumption and is kept as a hypothesis, although the statement does not need it.
-- source:
--   Beck, Eldar, Sparsity Constrained Nonlinear Optimization: Optimality Conditions and Algorithms, SIAM J. Optim. (2013), doi:10.1137/120869778 (source: arXiv:1203.4580v1), p. 19, Lemma 3.2

import Definitions.Def_SparseNLO_Greedy_Method

open Filter Topology

namespace SparseNLO.Greedy

/-- Lemma 3.2 (p. 19): along every run of the greedy sparse-simplex method,
`f(xᵏ⁺¹) ≤ f(xᵏ)` for every `k ≥ 0`, with equality if and only if `xᵏ = xᵏ⁺¹` and `xᵏ` is a
CW-minimum. -/
theorem lemma_3_2
    {n s : ℕ} (f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 1 f)
    (hbdd : ∃ γ : ℝ, ∀ x, γ ≤ f x) (hs : 0 < s) (hsn : s < n)
    (x : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (hrun : IsGreedyRun f s x) :
    ∀ k : ℕ, f (x (k + 1)) ≤ f (x k) ∧
      (f (x (k + 1)) = f (x k) ↔ x k = x (k + 1) ∧ SparseNLO.CWOpt.IsCWMin f s (x k)) := by sorry

end SparseNLO.Greedy
